<h1><span lang="EN-GB">SURFA Card Related Problems</span></h1>
<hr class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Some common problems associated with the SURFA PCI card.</span></p>
<h2>MMIB LEDs are not illuminated:</h2>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">LEDs will not be illuminated if SURFA PCI board is not connected to the MMIB.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">This will also be the case if power lead is not connected to SURFA PCI board inside PC.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">The SURFA PCI 2 uses "resettable" fuses. In the event of a short-circuit, power down the PC for a few minutes to reset the fuses.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Note" id="p1"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">: Be sure to fix the short-circuit before restarting the PC.</span></p>
<p class="Normal" style="font-weight:normal;">&#160;</p>
<h2>"FIFO error" appears in sensor view</h2>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This is a SURFA PCI problem caused by there being insufficient bandwidth on the PCI bus. The most common reason is some other PCI device or problem with the drivers for it.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Solution</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">: Check all other PCI devices, update to the latest drivers. If necessary, replace with alternatives.</span></p>
<p>&#160;</p>
<h2><span lang="EN-GB"><span lang="EN-GB">W</span>rong sensor recognition</span></h2>
<p>The MM Z system is not recognised properly by software and error loading SURFA PCI drivers message is displayed. No SURFA PCI devices can be found in device manager.</p>
<p><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Solution</b></span>: Most probably the MMIB-DL I/O cable has been partially disconnected or MMIB-DL power supply has been unplugged. In this case it is recommended to switch off and on both PC and MMIB-DL in order to restore properly connections between them. Ensure the MMIB-DL is powered up first whenever the PC is started up or shut down.</p>

